Promote the long-standing -O3 -funroll-loops working-tree edit (in CMakeLists.txt
since wave-33 slot 0128 timeframe) to a numbered patch. Was previously tracked
as a working-tree edit per slot 0128's commit-message note ('intentionally NOT
in this patch — predates slot 0128 and is tracked separately at the team-lead's
discretion; next-session hygiene: bake into a numbered patch'). Network outage
2026-05-12 rolled back the working-tree edit, surfacing the need to promote.

The wave-33 / 34 / 35 perf patches (0128 / 0130 / 0131 / 0132) all measured
their gains at -O3 -funroll-loops + reference this flag set as the build
baseline in their commit messages. Without this promotion, build chains in
future sessions would build at -O2 and the prior measurements would not
replicate.

-O3 raises binary size modestly but the P54C i486 cache trade has been
net-positive on every wave since slot 0128. -funroll-loops similarly nets +1
to +3 fps from inner-loop hot paths in tile blit + audio mix.

Slot 0133 is intentionally skipped; reserved for a possible Cirrus 5434 BLT
async backdrop flush patch if probe-engineer's BLTASYNC v3 investigation
finds a working BULK_COPY register sequence. See /tmp/wave-36/slot-0133-body/
for pre-stage (gitignored).
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index a17af75..dc26f17 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -157,7 +157,18 @@ add_definitions("-Wall")
 # nlohmann::json::parse, plus 5 unguarded parse sites that would convert
 # survivable log+continue to abort under -fno-exceptions + JSON_NOEXCEPTION).
 if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "MSDOS" OR CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER MATCHES "msdosdjgpp")
-    add_compile_options(-march=i486 -mtune=pentium -O2 -fno-rtti)
+    # slot 0134 wave-36: promote -O3 -funroll-loops from working-tree edit to
+    # patch-captured form. The wave-33 / 34 / 35 perf patches (0128 / 0130 /
+    # 0131 / 0132) all measured their gains at -O3 -funroll-loops and their
+    # commit messages reference this flag set as the build baseline. Was a
+    # working-tree edit per slot 0128's "tracked separately at the team-lead's
+    # discretion; next-session hygiene: bake into a numbered patch" note;
+    # post-outage rollback (2026-05-12) wiped the working-tree edit and
+    # surfaced the need to promote. -O3 raises code-size modestly but the
+    # P54C i486 cache trade has been net-positive on every wave since slot
+    # 0128. -funroll-loops similarly nets +1 to +3 fps from inner-loop hot
+    # paths in tile blit + audio mix.
+    add_compile_options(-march=i486 -mtune=pentium -O3 -funroll-loops -fno-rtti)
     add_compile_definitions(NXE_DOS)
 endif()
 
